00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,300
You think this turquoise water is photoshopped.
{\fs13}I'm your China Travel Expert

2
00:00:03,300 --> 00:00:06,800
It's real — Huanglong, high in the mountains of Sichuan, China.

3
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:10,300
The pools are built by calcite, a mineral the spring water leaves behind.

4
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:13,500
That mineral, plus the light, gives the water its colour — no filter.

5
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:16,800
Over 3,000 metres up. UNESCO listed since 1992. Too perfect to be real? Tell me below.
